Example 1 – basic division
  Calculate &frac{3}{4} ÷ &frac{1}{2}
  Keep: &frac{3}{4}. Flip: &frac{1}{2} becomes &frac{2}{1}
  Multiply: &frac{3}{4} × &frac{2}{1} = &frac{6}{4}
  Simplify: &frac{6}{4} = &frac{3}{2} = 1&frac{1}{2}
  = 1&frac{1}{2}
  (Flip the second fraction then multiply across.)

Example 2 – dividing by a whole number
  Calculate &frac{2}{5} ÷ 3
  Write 3 as &frac{3}{1}
  Flip: &frac{3}{1} becomes &frac{1}{3}
  Multiply: &frac{2}{5} × &frac{1}{3} = &frac{2}{15}
  = &frac{2}{15}
  (A whole number n = &frac{n}{1}. Its reciprocal is &frac{1}{n}.)

Keep, Flip, Change. Simplify your answer.

(a) &frac{2}{3} ÷ &frac{4}{5}
(b) &frac{3}{8} ÷ &frac{3}{4}
(c) &frac{4}{9} ÷ &frac{2}{3}
(d) &frac{5}{6} ÷ &frac{2}{9}

Calculate. Give answers in simplest form.

(a) &frac{7}{8} ÷ &frac{7}{4}
(b) 5 ÷ &frac{1}{3}
(c) &frac{9}{10} ÷ &frac{3}{5}
(d) 2&frac{1}{2} ÷ &frac{5}{6}
(e) &frac{1}{4} ÷ &frac{3}{8}

✓ &frac{2}{3} ÷ &frac{1}{4} = &frac{2}{3} × &frac{4}{1} = &frac{8}{3}
✗ Flip the first fraction when dividing
✓ Reciprocal of &frac{3}{5} is &frac{5}{3}
✗ &frac{1}{2} ÷ &frac{1}{4} = &frac{1}{8}
✓ Dividing by &frac{1}{2} is the same as multiplying by 2

